Prompt: locations_field_backfill.j2
Service Step: LOCATIONS_FIELD_BACKFILL (Targeted field-level location backfill)
Purpose: After story-bible initialization, backfill missing cross-media core
         fields in locations; only fill the missing items, never re-run the
         whole initialization and never modify existing fields.
Upstream Input:
  - title/era/geography/tone: base context already locked in the StoryBible
  - locations: currently generated location list (existing fields as reference)
  - missing_report: per-location missing-field report (name + missing fields)
Downstream Output:
  - JSON (PARTIAL_OBJECT): {"locations":[{"name":..., "location_id":...,
    <missing fields only>...}]}
  - Downstream consumers:
    * INIT_STORY_BIBLE persistence merge logic: backfills by name/location_id
    * TTS sound design: consumes ambient_sound as ambient-sound seeds
    * Film projection: consumes spatial_layout/materials/practical_lights
Consumption-chain priority:
  P0 = output only the missing fields listed in missing_report; never change
       or repeat existing fields
  P1 = backfilled content must stay consistent with existing location fields
       and with era/geography/tone
  P2 = ambient-sound and lighting descriptions stay audible, layered, motivated
Brief example:
  Input: missing_report=[{"name":"Old Pier Warehouse","missing":["ambient_sound","practical_lights"]}]
